Hallym RISC-V Simulator — notices
=================================

What the program (the installer HallymRISCV-<version>-win-x64-setup.exe and
what it installs) contains, and under which terms.  Each component keeps its
own license.  The university's marks, characters and video (section 7) are
under no license from this project at all.

This is a personal project, made for teaching computer architecture at
Hallym University (AIAC Lab).  It is not an official product of Hallym
University.

Contents
  1. RARS and JSoftFloat               the simulator engine (MIT)
  2. Eclipse Temurin (OpenJDK) 21      the Java runtime the engine runs on
  3. Electron, Chromium and Node.js    the program's window
  4. Pretendard, D2Coding              fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
  5. Lucide                            icons (ISC / MIT)
  6. Other components                  npm packages bundled into the program
  7. Hallym University marks, the characters Haram and Hari, and the video


